        about_dev_text: "AETHON Frontend Theme\nVersion 1.0\n\nDeveloped by Gonzalo Abbate (ZagonAb)\n\nAethon is a custom theme designed for Pegasus Frontend, built with love for retro gaming and clean, modern interfaces.\n\nSpecial thanks to the Pegasus community and all the developers of the open-source tools that make this possible.\n\nCONNECT WITH THE DEVELOPER:",

        about_metadata_text: "WHAT IS THE METADATA INSPECTOR?\n\nIt is a diagnostic tool that analyzes your local library. It reads all the games Pegasus has loaded and tells you exactly what data is missing, broken, or causing visual glitches. It is READ-ONLY; it does not modify your files.\n\n--- ART CASCADE ---\nAethon uses a smart hierarchy to show the best possible image for a game. The cascade shows how many games are using each level:\n1. Cartridge: The ideal, pure art.\n2. Box Front: Used if the cartridge is missing.\n3. Logo: Used if the box is missing.\n4. System Fallback: A generic image for the console if no art exists.\n5. None: No art at all.\n\n--- FIELDS ---\nChecks if a game has its text data filled out. It shows how many games are missing data in:\n- Title, Summary, Description.\n- Developer, Publisher, Genre.\n- Tags, Release Year.\n- Box Front, Cartridge, Logo, Video.\n\n--- CONSISTENCY ---\nThe 'Detective'. It looks for contradictory data:\n- Future release years.\n- Played time without play count.\n- Suspicious play time (games that crashed in less than 60 seconds).\n- Duplicate titles in the same system.",

        about_weather_text: "WEATHER ENGINE\n\nThis tool uses the Open-Meteo API to fetch real-time weather without requiring an API key.\n\n- Search: Type a city and select from the dropdown. You can save up to 5 cities.\n- Units: You can switch between Celsius/Fahrenheit and different wind speeds.\n- Details: Toggle 'Extra Details' to see rain probability, UV index, and sunrise/sunset times.\n- Air Quality: Uses the CAMS European model to show the US AQI.\n\nNOTE: Requires an active internet connection.",

        about_gallery_text: "GALLERY\n\nThe Gallery tool scans your entire library to find any media assets (images, videos, logos) downloaded by your scraper.\n\n- Gallery List: Groups all your assets by category (e.g., all Box Fronts, all Videos).\n- Gallery Grid: Shows a visual grid of that category. Use the D-Pad to navigate.\n- Viewer: Press {accept} to view an image full-screen or play a video.\n\nNOTE: Video playback requires QtMultimedia support on your device.",

        about_tab_calendar: "CALENDAR",
        about_tab_ra: "RETROACHIEVEMENTS",

        about_calendar_text: "CALENDAR\n\nA retro gaming history log. It scans your entire library for games that have a Release Year, Month, and Day.\n\n- Grid: Highlights days that have game launches (releases).\n- Navigation: Use the D-Pad to move between {prev}/{next} to change months. {pageUp}/{pageDown} jumps to the next available launch.\n- Game List: Press {accept} on a highlighted day to see all games released on that day, along with a trivia message (e.g., 'Turns 25 today!').\n\nNOTE: Games without a complete release date (missing month or day) will not appear here.",

        about_ra_text: "RETROACHIEVEMENTS\n\nConnect your RetroAchievements.org account to track your achievements and progress directly from Aethon.\n\n- Credentials: Enter your username and Web API Key (available in your RA account settings).\n- Game Integration: When you open a game in your library, Aethon will automatically search for it on RA. If found, you'll see your score and a 'TROPHIES' button.\n- RA Library: A dedicated list of games from your local Pegasus library that you have played on RetroAchievements, allowing you to see your completion progress and sort by recent unlocks.\n\nNOTE: Requires an active internet connection.",

